scribe the bug**\r\nAccording to the Quarkus guide it should be possible to set the datasource password via an environment variable QUARKUS_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD\r\nhttps://quarkus.io/guides/application-configuration-guide\r\n\r\nIn my case (with a Postgres DB) this was not enough, I has to add the following line to the application.properties file:\r\nquarkus.datasource.password=QUARKUS_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD\r\n\r\nWithout this line I got a Postgres exception saying the password was not provided.\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nEither setting the environment variable QUARKUS_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD should be enough or the additional line in the application.properties should be added to the guide.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nWhen adding a startup bean I was able to verify that only setting the environment property was enough to inject the datasource password with a ConfigProperty:\r\n@ConfigProperty(name=\"quarkus.datasource.password\")\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"dmlloyd","id":124581,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDU4MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124581?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd","html_url":"https://github.com/dmlloyd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlloyd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/2760/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":